Swedish keywords for the Scala compiler (Kojo).

DRAFT — the Swedish keyword strings below are AI-suggested starting points and
MUST be reviewed by a native Swedish speaker (see scala-sv/README). The
mechanism mirrors scala-tr/turkish-keywords.patch exactly.

Generated against the pristine scala/scala v2.13.18 sources, so it applies to a
clean checkout of that tag:

    git clone https://github.com/scala/scala ~/src/scala-2.13.18
    cd ~/src/scala-2.13.18 && git checkout v2.13.18
    git apply <kojo-clone>/scala-sv/swedish-keywords.patch
    sbt 'set Global/baseVersionSuffix := ""' dist/mkPack

The change to Main.scala is only a diagnostic println and is not required; the
keywords come from Scanners.scala (the Swedish entries go FIRST in allKeywords,
so compiler errors still report the English keyword) and StdNames.scala.

--- a/src/compiler/scala/tools/nsc/Main.scala
+++ b/src/compiler/scala/tools/nsc/Main.scala
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
   override def newCompiler(): Global = Global(settings)
 
   override def doCompile(compiler: Global): Unit = {
+    println("[Kojo] Scala Compiler v2.13.18 with Swedish keywords")
     if (settings.resident.value) resident(compiler)
     else super.doCompile(compiler)
   }
